Algorithm
Start.
Read the number of disks n.
If n == 1, move the disk directly from the source rod to the destination rod.
Otherwise:
Move the top n−1 disks from the source rod to the auxiliary rod.
Move the largest disk from the source rod to the destination rod.
Move the n−1 disks from the auxiliary rod to the destination rod.

Print the minimum number of moves using the formula:

Minimum Moves=2^n -1
Stop.
